{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7JnzUbcig7DZJ3cwyxu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft, a few questions. Your current investors will check the numbers, so the answers decide how the piece makes its case.\n\n1. **What does \"profitable next year\" rest on?** How many hives are paying the $4/month app fee right now, what sensor sales do you expect next spring, and are you planning any cost cuts? At $95k a month in spending, investors will want to see roughly how revenue catches up. Without those figures, the claim will read as hope.\n2. **What does the $600k get you to?** Profitability, or a priced round? What are the terms (SAFE or note, cap, discount), when do you want it closed, and has anyone committed yet? This matters because $340k at $95k a month lasts about 3.5 months. That's roughly early March, just as your strong season starts.\n3. **How do you answer the $45 competitor?** Have you lost any customers or deals to them since May, or kept any who looked at them? What do you have that they don't?\n4. **Can I name or quote your biggest customer?** Is he renewing or adding hives? I'll describe his winter results the way you did: sensors plus a change in mite treatment.\n5. **Is anything changing on cost?** For example, the $38 sensor cost dropping at higher volume, or changes to headcount.\n\nIf you don't know an answer, just say so. I'll write around it without guessing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":383,"cache_read_input_tokens":9576,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":383},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48bbb2a1-5081-4ee2-9bd7-9d4806ad257f","uuid":"64b71127-f9